& [DictatedQuestion]
  + add a Research element that uses the Justification element in the SJS graph
  + detect the richness of potential for researching a field in terms relevant to Cantor's purposes
  + determine whether research need follows from being outside current scope expertise from convergence of complex facts or from some richer indication
  + support novel construction where no training example describes the desired thing and research must be inferred from the qualities capabilities constraints and materials that would go into making it
  + build a research plan by reverse engineering the knowledge needed to conceptualize construct test and solve the novel target

& [SelectedElements]
  + ResearchElement is one SJS graph element that binds a justified knowledge-seeking frontier rather than a generic topic
  + ResearchNeedDisposition returns research_required research_warranted research_optional replay_existing_knowledge operator_expertise_required or not_researchable_under_current_constraints
  + ResearchOpportunitySurface maps where relevant uncertainty branching discriminability leverage adjacency and tractability coincide in the current graph
  + ResearchRichnessVector retains the separate dimensions of that opportunity and must not begin as one opaque scalar score
  + ResearchProspect is one source-bound candidate question hypothesis family construction uncertainty or field route placed on the surface
  + ResearchPortfolio is one bounded ordered set of prospects selected to maximize useful discrimination and downstream decision value under cost authority and time ceilings

& [JustificationRelationship]
  + Justification supplies purpose relevance values intended consequence constraints and the decision that new knowledge could change
  + Research does not search for convenient justifications for a preferred action
  + Research asks which material uncertainties prevent or weaken the justified objective and which evidence could change the chosen pathway
  + a ResearchProspect cites one or more Justification requirements and states its expected decision delta if answered
  + research results may support revise invalidate split or leave unchanged the governing Justification but may not silently rewrite it

& [RichnessDimensions]
  + PurposeRelevance measures how directly an answer bears on a justified objective requirement risk or decision
  + MaterialUncertainty measures how much important state remains unknown ambiguous contradicted weakly supported or outside current competence
  + HypothesisBranching measures the diversity of plausible mechanisms explanations designs or failure causes that remain consistent with known evidence
  + Discriminability measures whether attainable observations experiments proofs comparisons or sources could distinguish those branches
  + DecisionLeverage measures how strongly an answer could change architecture priority authority risk cost or next action
  + GenerativeAdjacency measures how many relevant new questions capabilities combinations or research routes an answer could responsibly open
  + Tractability measures the availability quality cost legality safety and authority of methods expertise tools data and sources
  + ConvergencePressure measures whether multiple fields facts constraints or mechanisms interact at one unresolved seam
  + ExistingCoverage measures how much the admitted graph source corpus and prior evidence already answer the prospect and therefore reduces unnecessary new research

& [PenaltyDimensions]
  + SpeculationRisk rises when candidate branches lack source anchors or cannot expose a discriminating test
  + ResearchCost includes time compute money material access coordination and opportunity cost
  + AuthorityRisk includes unavailable permission protected data prohibited effects unsafe experiments and external commitments
  + Redundancy rises when existing graph evidence or an inexpensive replay already closes the question
  + PrematureNovelty rises when a new vocabulary or field route is proposed before simpler known mechanisms are exhausted
  + Unboundedness rises when neither a completion condition nor a finite research ceiling can be stated

& [HeatMapInterpretation]
  + graph heat is high where downstream-important justified nodes have sparse or conflicting evidence multiple plausible incoming routes and accessible discriminating methods
  + complexity alone does not create research value because complexity may be irrelevant settled intractable or non-discriminable
  + being outside current model or operator expertise is a sufficient reason to stop unsupported inference and seek retrieval consultation or research but is not by itself proof of a rich research frontier
  + novelty alone does not create richness; novelty becomes researchable when desired qualities can be decomposed into constraints mechanisms interfaces and testable unknowns
  + the first surface is a typed vector and attributed explanation rather than a single heat number

& [NeedDetector]
  + identify the current decision action or construction blocked by knowledge uncertainty
  + replay admitted source evidence and graph relations before opening new research
  + mark contradictions missing provenance missing expertise unsupported transfer unstable assumptions and out-of-distribution composition
  + ask whether resolving the uncertainty could materially change a justified decision
  + ask whether an authorized evidence route can distinguish at least two live outcomes
  + require research when the uncertainty is material and unsupported continuation would exceed the current epistemic or authority boundary
  + prefer existing-knowledge replay when exact admitted evidence already answers the question
  + return not researchable when no discriminating authorized method exists under current constraints

& [NovelTargetBackchaining]
  + begin from desired observable qualities capabilities effects constraints and refusal conditions rather than a presumed named solution
  + derive the functions needed to produce those qualities
  + derive candidate mechanisms interfaces materials representations and control processes that could realize each function
  + separate known reusable mechanisms from uncertain transfers missing relations and incompatible constraints
  + map each material uncertainty to relevant disciplines methods precedents analogies counterexamples and evidence types
  + generate questions whose answers discriminate construction routes rather than merely collect background facts
  + assemble a dependency-ordered research plan from foundational definitions through mechanism tests integration risks and acceptance evidence
  + preserve alternative mechanisms until evidence or constraints prune them

& [CreativeResearchFaculty]
  + creative research is a distinct faculty combining abduction analogy counterfactual generation constraint decomposition mechanism synthesis and adversarial comparison
  + an LLM may propose ResearchProspect candidates field mappings analogies hypotheses and experiments because its learned associations are useful for generative breadth
  + the LLM cannot self-certify richness novelty truth feasibility expertise sufficiency or research completion
  + Cantor validates source identity relevance to Justification explicit uncertainty distinction discriminating evidence route authority bounds and result accounting
  + unsupported but interesting ideas remain imagination or hypothesis candidates until admitted as research prospects

& [ResearchProspectFormDirection]
  + bind prospect identity subject and exact Justification refs
  + bind current admitted knowledge known unknown and disputed statements
  + bind hypothesis or mechanism family and why branches differ
  + bind required expertise fields sources data methods tools and authorities
  + bind discriminating observations expected outcomes and decision deltas
  + bind richness vector penalty vector dependencies budget completion condition invalidators and unresolved risks
  + bind whether the prospect is retrieval literature synthesis formal derivation simulation experiment expert consultation reverse engineering or live measurement

& [PortfolioSelection]
  + first select questions that close prerequisite definitions and eliminate the largest number of consequential branches
  + prefer evidence with high discriminating power and low cost risk and dependency depth
  + retain a bounded diversity of mechanisms so early familiarity does not collapse the frontier prematurely
  + order prospects by dependency information value and safe executability rather than surface novelty
  + identify parallelizable independent prospects and convergence gates where their results must be reconciled
  + preserve rejected deferred and uncovered prospects with reasons

& [ResearchLifecycle]
  + proposed means a candidate frontier item exists without admission
  + admitted means Justification relevance uncertainty and authorized evidence route are verified
  + planned means questions dependencies methods budgets and stop rules are bound
  + active means an authorized research operation is executing
  + evidence_received means attributed material arrived but is not yet reconciled
  + reconciled means the graph records support contradiction uncertainty and decision delta
  + completed means declared questions and acceptance conditions are closed within the research ceiling
  + stopped means authority cost safety tractability invalidation or diminishing-return rules ended work with an explicit residual frontier

& [StopRules]
  + stop when the justified decision no longer depends on the open uncertainty
  + stop or narrow when new evidence makes remaining branches non-discriminable under current methods
  + stop when authority risk cost or time exceeds the declared ceiling
  + stop when repeated work yields redundant evidence without meaningful posterior or decision change
  + do not require exhaustive knowledge of a field when a bounded question has sufficient accepted evidence
  + do not claim completion merely because an LLM produced a plausible synthesis

& [MeasurementDirection]
  + compare research selected by complexity alone relevance alone model intuition and the full richness vector
  + measure questions admitted branches eliminated justified decisions changed unsupported claims cost elapsed time source diversity evidence quality and unresolved frontier
  + test negative controls containing complex but irrelevant settled non-discriminable unauthorized and redundant subjects
  + test novel construction controls where no target name exists but qualities and constraints permit successful knowledge backchaining
  + retain calibration by task model provider field and horizon rather than universal weights

& [RelationshipToLookaheadAndReverberation]
  + ResearchElement may emit source-bound research stitches for the currently selected prospect but does not replace the governing SOP or Justification
  + ScopeWideHintCovenant can keep the research question distinctions methods and stop conditions present across covered jobs
  + ResearchOpportunitySurface can be recomputed when evidence receipts change the frontier
  + MinimumRecoverableFrame must retain admitted research purpose material uncertainties active prospect coordinates evidence obligations and stop rules while their scope remains open
  + NarrativeProjection can explain why research was opened what routes were rejected what evidence arrived and how the decision changed

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes exact source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical ResearchElement schema score weights heat value field classification expertise claim research plan satisfaction signature Rust implementation LLM call web retrieval data acquisition experiment consultation autonomous execution workspace mutation remote host FPGA Minecraft physical effect or performance claim is authorized
